        '1.42': "May Supathā protect my road and Kṣemakarī my path; may Mahālakṣmī protect me at the king's gate, and Vijayā, present everywhere, on all sides.",
        '1.43': "Whatever place is left unguarded, not covered by this armour, protect all of it for me, O Devī Jayantī, destroyer of sin.",
        '1.44': "One who desires his own good should not go even a single step without this armour. One who is always covered by it, wherever he goes,",
